{
  "title": "Modulation",
  "startSide": "back",
  "learned": [
    "CV: voltages that turn knobs for you",
    "An LFO on the filter and on the pitch",
    "Attenuverter: scale and flip a voltage",
    "A square LFO for a trill"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "A control voltage (CV) is a voltage that turns a knob for you. Audio wiggles hundreds of times a second; CV usually moves slowly. In this lesson an LFO, a slow oscillator, moves other modules.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch TRI of the LFO to FREQ CV of the filter.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "output": "Tri"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCF",
          "input": "Freq CV"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "LFO",
            "output": "Tri"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "VCF",
            "input": "Freq CV"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn up CUTOFF CV of the filter. That knob sets how far the LFO moves the cutoff: the filter now breathes.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "VCF",
          "param": "Cutoff CV"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "VCF",
          "param": "Cutoff CV"
        },
        "min": 30
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn RATE of the LFO. Slow, it is a sweep; fast, it becomes a wobble.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "param": "Rate"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "LFO",
          "param": "Rate"
        },
        "moved": 0.2
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Now the pitch. Press Tab and patch SIN of the LFO to FM of the oscillator.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "output": "Sin"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCO",
          "input": "FM"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "LFO",
            "output": "Sin"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "VCO",
            "input": "FM"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn FM of the oscillator up just a little: vibrato. Too much and the pitch swings wildly.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "VCO",
          "param": "Frequency modulation"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "VCO",
          "param": "Frequency modulation"
        },
        "min": 3,
        "max": 30
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "An attenuverter scales and flips a voltage. Press Tab, patch SIN of the LFO to IN 1 of the attenuverter, and OUT 1 of the attenuverter to FM of the oscillator (it replaces the old cable).",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "output": "Sin"
        },
        {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "input": "In 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "output": "Out 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCO",
          "input": "FM"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "LFO",
                "output": "Sin"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Attenuverter",
                "input": "In 1"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Attenuverter",
                "output": "Out 1"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "VCO",
                "input": "FM"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn GAIN 1 of the attenuverter. Left of the middle the vibrato is upside down; at the middle it stops.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "param": "Row 1 gain"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "param": "Row 1 gain"
        },
        "moved": 0.1
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and patch SQR of the LFO to IN 1 of the attenuverter; the old cable goes.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "output": "Sqr"
        },
        {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "input": "In 1"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "LFO",
            "output": "Sqr"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "Attenuverter",
            "input": "In 1"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn GAIN 1 up. A square wave jumps between two voltages, so the pitch jumps between two notes: a trill.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "param": "Row 1 gain"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Attenuverter",
          "param": "Row 1 gain"
        },
        "min": 1.5
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Compare the two worlds on the scope: press Tab, patch SIN of the LFO to IN 1 (the envelope's cable goes) and OUT 1 of the amplifier to IN 2.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "LFO",
          "output": "Sin"
        },
        {
          "module": "Scope",
          "input": "In 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "VCA",
          "output": "Out 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Scope",
          "input": "In 2"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "LFO",
                "output": "Sin"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Scope",
                "input": "In 1"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "VCA",
                "output": "Out 1"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Scope",
                "input": "In 2"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Audio and CV are the same thing: voltages, only at different speeds. Any output can drive any input, so try your own connections. Press Next to finish.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
